# Files kept in the repository but NOT shipped in the published archive.
#
# The rest of `test/` ships and runs from a hosted install: those tests are
# about this runtime's own behaviour, and the two corpus fixtures they need are
# copied into `test/fixtures/corpus/` for exactly that reason.
#
# These two cannot be, and the reason is the same for both: their subject IS the
# shared nine-language conformance corpus, which lives in `tom_som_conformance`
# and is not published.
#
#   conformance_test.dart  — the Dart side of the cross-language harness. It
#     replays the committed corpus tables; without them there is nothing to
#     replay.
#   enum_coverage_test.dart — proves every guarded enum constant is exercised by
#     a corpus table. Copying the tables in would make it assert against a copy,
#     which is the opposite of what it is for.
#
# Both build their paths from `Directory.current` plus components rather than
# from a `../` literal, so the shipped-path scanner cannot see them; a
# hosted-install simulation is what found them.
test/conformance_test.dart
test/enum_coverage_test.dart
